/-!
# Candidate coordinates and spanning forest for the Held representative

The 24 components are the lists retained in `InnerNormalizer/Source/orbits.json`.
Each vertex has a component number, an index within that component, and a
parent reached by one of the four published generator words. The maximal
candidate tree depth is nine. Packed integers are lookup data, not proofs;
`Checks` certifies the coordinates and edges, and `Actions` connects the
four action tables to the actual Held elements.

Source: ATLAS HeG1-p2058B0 and HeG1-max3W1, and GLS3 Table 5.3p.
The reproducer is `OrbitCertificate/Source/generate.py`.
-/

namespace Held.LocalPairs.SylowGeometry.Calculations.InnerNormalizer.OrbitCertificate

@[expose] public def color (x : Fin 2058) : Fin 24 :=
  ⟨(( >>> (5 * x.val)) % 32) % 24, Nat.mod_lt _ (by decide)⟩

